in Iran revolutionary sentiment flows  through its streets including those of  the capital Tehran hear vast crowds  descend on a Central Square to call for  the removal of the regime  in corvae residents silently marched  through the town the police watch from  the side while shops and businesses  throughout the country have shut their  doors the authorities accuse their  opponents of waging a war against God  the first protester from this popular  Rebellion has been hanged mohsin shikari  was arrested in September then sentenced  to death for injuring a security guard  here's an alleged witness speaking at  his trial  the Iranian Judiciary produced a slick  video where shikari confesses to his  so-called crime the message here is  clear dissent is punishable by death  another 21 protesters faced the death  penalty it's thought unfortunately it  was expected because we know that  Iranian authorities use the death penalt  to spread fear the reason why people are  on the streets protesting is that this  barrier of fear is broken and now they  want to use executions to restore this  barrier  the protests in Iran were triggered by  the death of a 22 year old called Masa  amini she died in police custody after  she was arrested for wearing her hijab  incorrectly  but the execution of protesters is  unlikely to quell this Rebellion people  in Iran are even more angry at the  Iranian authorities now then they were  before the execution of shikari so I we  will Ex we are expecting more protests  The clerics Who Run Iran have been  rattled by public displays of defiance  but they won't give way without a fight  John Sparks Sky News
 

